1
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,633
London's office market moves every week.

2
00:00:06,233 --> 00:00:11,543
The evidence is scattered across agency
reports, public statistics, the news, and

3
00:00:11,543 --> 00:00:15,800
colleagues' inboxes, and every hand-off loses
a little of it.

4
00:00:16,400 --> 00:00:20,600
The London Office Market Agent keeps it in one
place, for the whole team.

5
00:00:22,600 --> 00:00:23,833
It does three jobs.

6
00:00:24,433 --> 00:00:27,900
Monitor watches the market, and summarises
what changed.

7
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:30,900
Copilot answers questions at any moment.

8
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,533
Team brief turns the week into a paper and a
slide deck.

9
00:00:36,533 --> 00:00:38,567
Every figure carries its source.

10
00:00:39,167 --> 00:00:43,067
Open data, such as Bank Rate and news, is
collected automatically.

11
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:49,537
Agency reports, whose terms forbid scraping,
are uploaded once by a colleague, and shared

12
00:00:49,537 --> 00:00:50,367
with everyone.

13
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:52,800
Our own deals stay internal.

14
00:00:54,800 --> 00:01:00,270
Behind the screen, a skill-based agent plans
its steps, and calls Python tools to read,

15
00:01:00,270 --> 00:01:01,967
check and analyse the data.

16
00:01:02,567 --> 00:01:06,200
When two figures disagree, it flags them for a
person to check.

17
00:01:06,800 --> 00:01:07,967
Nothing is hidden.

18
00:01:09,867 --> 00:01:11,067
Now, how to use it.

19
00:01:11,667 --> 00:01:13,800
Open the link, and pick your name.

20
00:01:14,400 --> 00:01:16,933
This proof of concept needs no password.

21
00:01:18,933 --> 00:01:22,533
Monitor opens with the team summary, then
today's signals.

22
00:01:23,133 --> 00:01:26,800
Each card says what moved, by how much, and
why it matters.

23
00:01:27,400 --> 00:01:32,667
Describe your job in one sentence, and For You
narrows the list to the submarkets you follow.

24
00:01:33,267 --> 00:01:36,433
Found something for the board? Press Add to
brief.

25
00:01:38,433 --> 00:01:42,533
Got a question? Ask Copilot in plain English,
or in Chinese.

26
00:01:43,133 --> 00:01:45,767
Here, we ask it to compare two submarkets.

27
00:01:46,367 --> 00:01:51,437
The agent works through its steps, then
replies with a table, charts, and the source

28
00:01:51,437 --> 00:01:52,567
behind every number.

29
00:01:53,167 --> 00:01:57,400
Share to team passes the answer to your
colleagues, exactly as written.

30
00:01:59,400 --> 00:02:01,033
Heard something from a broker?

31
00:02:01,633 --> 00:02:07,583
Share the link or the tip. It is filed,
de-duplicated, and labelled as unverified, so

32
00:02:07,583 --> 00:02:10,533
what one colleague hears, the whole team
knows.

33
00:02:11,133 --> 00:02:13,633
On Sources, upload an agency report.

34
00:02:14,233 --> 00:02:19,333
The agent reads every page, and any doubtful
figure waits for a person to check.

35
00:02:21,333 --> 00:02:23,533
At the end of the week, open Team brief.

36
00:02:24,133 --> 00:02:28,643
The paper is already written from the signals
your team chose, with a footnote for every

37
00:02:28,643 --> 00:02:29,300
figure.

38
00:02:29,900 --> 00:02:35,100
Download it in Word or PDF, or open Slides,
and change the deck simply by asking.

39
00:02:37,200 --> 00:02:42,910
One team, one set of numbers, and nothing lost
along the way, from Monday's news to Friday's

40
00:02:42,910 --> 00:02:43,800
board paper.

41
00:02:44,400 --> 00:02:49,333
Market figures shown are restated from Knight
Frank reports, for evaluation only.
